-- Mauritania service area.
--
-- One region, because the pilot serves the country. The merchant's
-- origin/destination restriction names it; setup.sh sets that from COVERAGE.
--
-- Boundary: Geofabrik's own .poly for africa/mauritania -- the polygon they cut
-- the OSM extract with -- simplified with ST_SimplifyPreserveTopology at
-- ~200 m, the same tolerance algeria-geofences.sql used.
--
-- Using THAT boundary rather than a fresh OSM admin relation is deliberate:
-- it makes "serviceable" mean exactly "inside the area our routing graph
-- covers". Two boundaries that agree almost everywhere disagree somewhere, and
-- that somewhere is found by a ride failing rather than by a test.
--
-- Note what serviceable therefore does NOT mean: Mauritania is 1 030 000 km2
-- and mostly Sahara. A point in the Majabat al-Koubra is serviceable and
-- several hundred kilometres from any driver. Same caveat as Tamanrasset in
-- the Algerian file.
--
-- SRID is 0, not 4326, to match the existing rows and the ST_Point() the
-- application builds -- PostGIS refuses ST_Contains across mismatched SRIDs.
--
-- Idempotent: safe to re-run.
--
-- NOTE: the merchant row is cached in Redis
-- (Main/src/Storage/CachedQueries/Merchant.hs). After changing coverage the
-- cache must be dropped or the API keeps serving the previous areas:
--     docker exec ny-redis redis-cli FLUSHALL
-- setup.sh does this automatically.
--
-- (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL.

BEGIN;

DELETE FROM atlas_app.geometry WHERE region = 'Mauritania';

